tweets.text:
Teaching robots to understand real physical space is like opening a door to a completely new world. traditional artificial intelligence models only see text and flat screens, but real machines must learn how to touch objects, move safely and interact with daily human environments.

@PrismaXai builds an open foundation to solve this training bottleneck. Through teleoperation, human operators step in to control robots and perform everyday actions. The system collects these visual experience and uses an automated Eval Engine to verify quality without slowing down the pipeline. Instead of leaving robots idle, Hardware owners can actively put their machines to work as productive data miners.

Every human interaction unlocks new skills for physical AI models. 
I created this new art showing our robot companions and @vivianrobotics uncovering hidden treasures on their journey.

When humans and machines cooperate building autonomous robotics fells like a real adventure.👍
@MaxC16134

